    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Key difference to remember: Fundamental Rights aim at establishing political democracy, whereas DPSPs aim at establishing social and economic democracy.",
        "Frequently tested judgment: Minerva Mills Case (1980) affirmed the harmony and balance between Part III (FRs) and Part IV (DPSPs).",
        "Directives added by the 42nd Amendment Act of 1976 (e.g., Article 39A - Free Legal Aid, Article 43A - Worker participation in management) are extremely high-yield for competitive exams."
      ],
